# Adaptive Macro Engine — v5 (Production-Grade)

## End-to-End Runtime Lifecycle

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A["① Profile → NutritionCalculator\n(daily targets)"] --> B["② Progressive DB Fetch\n(single query, fallback widening)"]
    B --> C["③ Pre-Group by meal_type\n(O(n) single pass)"]
    C --> D["④ Compute Initial Section Targets\n(weighted importance + goal shift)"]
    D --> E["⑤ Macro Conservation Enforcement\n(redistribute delta → Σ = daily)"]
    E --> F["⑥ Compute Deficits + Weights\n(directional amplification)"]
    F --> G["⑦ Adaptive Rejection Filter\n(progress-scaled bounds)"]
    G --> H["⑧ Starvation Recovery\n(if eligible < threshold)"]
    H --> I["⑨ Score Each Candidate\n(unified formula, asymmetric penalty)"]
    I --> J["⑩ Apply Macro Skew Penalty\n(goal-aware ideal ranges)"]
    J --> K["⑪ Deterministic Diversity\n(yesterday penalty → pool → seed shuffle)"]
    K --> L["⑫ Render 4 Options Per Section"]
    L --> M["⑬ User Selects → Re-Score\n(remaining recomputed, unselected sections updated)"]
    M --> N["⑭ All Selected → saveMeals()\n(existing flow, unchanged)"]
```

### Step-by-Step Execution Order

| Step | What | When Normalization? | When Conservation? | When Directional? | When Fallback? |
|------|------|--------------------|--------------------|-------------------|----------------|
| ① | `NutritionCalculator.calculateTargets(profile)` → `daily` | — | — | — | — |
| ② | Single Supabase query with calorie bounds; widen if < 2 per section | — | — | — | ✅ Steps 2a-2d |
| ③ | `groupBy(meal_type)` in memory | — | — | — | — |
| ④ | `initialSectionTarget()` with goal timing shifts | — | — | — | — |
| ⑤ | Redistribute delta so `Σ targets = daily` per macro | — | ✅ Here | — | — |
| ⑥ | `computeWeights()` with directional multipliers | ✅ Normalize weights here | — | ✅ Here | — |
| ⑦ | Reject meals outside `[lower×, upper×]` of sectionTarget.cal | — | — | — | — |
| ⑧ | If eligible < 4: relax skew → relax bounds → all candidates → AI | — | — | — | ✅ Here |
| ⑨ | `score()` with asymmetric deviation penalties | — | — | ✅ Here | — |
| ⑩ | `macroSkewPenalty()` with goal-aware ideal ranges | — | — | — | — |
| ⑪ | Yesterday penalty → pool sizing → deterministic shuffle | — | — | — | — |
| ⑫ | UI renders options | — | — | — | — |
| ⑬ | `onUserSelect()` → recompute `remaining` (getter) → re-run ⑥-⑪ for unselected | ✅ Each re-score | — | ✅ Each re-score | ✅ If starvation |
| ⑭ | `MealService.saveMeals()` — unchanged | — | — | — | — |

---

## Stability Invariants

Eight guarantees enforced at all times:

| # | Invariant | Enforcement |
|---|-----------|-------------|
| INV-1 | `score ∈ [0.0, 1.0]` | `clamp(1.0 - error, 0.0, 1.0)` after every score computation |
| INV-2 | `Σ weights = 1.0` | Division by `total` in `computeWeights()` |
| INV-3 | No division by zero | All denominators use `max(value, 0.01)` where `value` could be zero |
| INV-4 | `sectionTarget[macro] ≥ 0` | `max(0, remaining / remainingSections)` for each macro |
| INV-5 | `Σ initialTargets = daily` per macro | Conservation redistribution in Step ⑤ |
| INV-6 | `dynamicFactor > 0` | `baseFactor = 1.2`, all additive terms ≥ 0 |
| INV-7 | `skewPenalty ∈ [0.0, 0.3]` | [min(0.3, penalty)](file:///Users/adityamagar/Fitness-Geni/fitness_geni/lib/core/services/gemini_service.dart#10-172) cap |
| INV-8 | `remaining` consistent | Computed getter from `daily - Σ(selected meals)`, never stored |

