## ⑥ Weights: Deficit + Directional Amplification + Bounded Spread

### Deficit Computation

```
FUNCTION computeDeficits(remaining, daily):
  RETURN {
    cal:  remaining.cal  / max(daily.cal, 1),       // range ≈ [-0.5, 1.0]
    prot: remaining.prot / max(daily.prot, 0.01),
    carb: remaining.carb / max(daily.carbs, 0.01),
    fat:  remaining.fat  / max(daily.fats, 0.01),
  }
  // Negative = overconsumed.  Positive = still needed.
```

### Directional Amplification Table

```
                    Undershoot (deficit > 0)    Overshoot (deficit < 0)
Calories            1.0                         1.3
Protein             1.3                         0.8
Carbs               1.0                         1.1
Fats                0.9                         1.2
```

| Direction | Multiplier | Rationale |
|-----------|-----------|-----------|
| Cal overshoot 1.3 | Excess calories → fat storage; most damaging nutritional error |
| Prot undershoot 1.3 | Protein deficit → muscle loss; highest priority to recover |
| Prot overshoot 0.8 | Excess protein excreted; no harm, dampen response |
| Fat overshoot 1.2 | Calorie-dense; easy to cascade into calorie excess |
| Fat undershoot 0.9 | Mild fat deficit is tolerable short-term |
| Carb overshoot 1.1 | Moderate — can cause energy spikes but less harmful than cal/prot |
| Cal/Carb undershoot 1.0 | Neutral — slight deficit often acceptable |

```
FUNCTION directionalDeficit(deficit, macro):
  IF deficit >= 0:
    mult = undershootMultiplier[macro]
  ELSE:
    mult = overshootMultiplier[macro]
  RETURN |deficit| × mult
```

### Dynamic Factor (Bounded Spread)

```
FUNCTION computeDynamicFactor(completedSelections, deficits):
  progress = completedSelections / 3

  deficitValues = [
    directionalDeficit(deficits.cal, "cal"),
    directionalDeficit(deficits.prot, "prot"),
    directionalDeficit(deficits.carb, "carb"),
    directionalDeficit(deficits.fat, "fat"),
  ]
  spread = max(deficitValues) - min(deficitValues)

  // Bounded contribution: logarithmic scaling
  spreadContribution = log₂(1 + spread)
  // spread ∈ [0, ~2.0]
  // log₂(1+0) = 0.00
  // log₂(1+0.5) = 0.58
  // log₂(1+1.0) = 1.00
  // log₂(1+1.5) = 1.32
  // log₂(1+2.0) = 1.58   ← theoretical max
  // Sublinear growth prevents over-amplification at extreme imbalance

  baseFactor = 1.2
  RETURN baseFactor × (1.0 + progress + spreadContribution)
```

| Scenario | Progress | Spread | log₂(1+s) | Factor |
|----------|----------|--------|-----------|--------|
| Initial, balanced | 0.0 | 0.0 | 0.00 | 1.20 |
| Lunch, mild imbalance | 0.33 | 0.3 | 0.38 | 2.05 |
| Snack, moderate imbalance | 0.67 | 0.6 | 0.68 | 2.82 |
| Dinner, balanced | 1.00 | 0.1 | 0.14 | 2.57 |
| Dinner, severe imbalance | 1.00 | 1.0 | 1.00 | 3.60 |

### Full Weight Computation

```
FUNCTION computeWeights(deficits, goal, completedSelections):
  dynamicFactor = computeDynamicFactor(completedSelections, deficits)

  // Directional effective deficits
  eff_cal  = directionalDeficit(deficits.cal, "cal")
  eff_prot = directionalDeficit(deficits.prot, "prot")
  eff_carb = directionalDeficit(deficits.carb, "carb")
  eff_fat  = directionalDeficit(deficits.fat, "fat")

  // Raw weights
  w_cal  = 1.0 + eff_cal  × dynamicFactor
  w_prot = 1.0 + eff_prot × dynamicFactor
  w_carb = 1.0 + eff_carb × dynamicFactor
  w_fat  = 1.0 + eff_fat  × dynamicFactor

  // Goal bias (capped at 0.5)
  IF goal == "weight_loss":
    w_prot += 0.5;  w_fat += 0.2
  ELSE IF goal == "bulking":
    w_carb += 0.4;  w_cal += 0.3

  // Normalize (INV-2)
  total = w_cal + w_prot + w_carb + w_fat
  RETURN { cal: w_cal/total, prot: w_prot/total, carb: w_carb/total, fat: w_fat/total }

  // INV-2 proof: Σ (w_i / total) = total / total = 1.0 ✓
  // Ratio preservation: w_a > w_b → w_a/total > w_b/total ✓
  // Dominance: if eff_prot = 1.3 and eff_carb = 0.3 at dinner (factor=3.6):
  //   w_prot = 1 + 1.3×3.6 + 0.5 = 6.18
  //   w_carb = 1 + 0.3×3.6 = 2.08
  //   ratio = 6.18 / 2.08 = 2.97× → protein dominates ✓
```

