## ⑦ Adaptive Rejection + ⑧ Starvation Recovery

### Rejection Bounds

```
progress = completedSelections / 3
upperMult(progress) = 2.0 - 0.5 × progress     // 2.0 → 1.5
lowerMult(progress) = 0.2 + 0.2 × progress     // 0.2 → 0.4
```

### Starvation Recovery Chain (deterministic)

```
FUNCTION getEligible(candidates, sectionTarget, progress, goal):
  upper = sectionTarget.cal × upperMult(progress)
  lower = sectionTarget.cal × lowerMult(progress)

  // LEVEL 0: Full filtering
  eligible = candidates.filter(m => m.cal >= lower AND m.cal <= upper)
  IF eligible.length >= 4: RETURN (eligible, level: 0)

  // LEVEL 1: Widen bounds by 50%
  wideUpper = sectionTarget.cal × (upperMult(progress) + 0.5)
  wideLower = sectionTarget.cal × max(0.1, lowerMult(progress) - 0.1)
  eligible = candidates.filter(m => m.cal >= wideLower AND m.cal <= wideUpper)
  IF eligible.length >= 4: RETURN (eligible, level: 1)

  // LEVEL 2: Remove calorie filter entirely
  eligible = candidates    // all meals of this meal_type
  IF eligible.length >= 2: RETURN (eligible, level: 2)

  // LEVEL 3: AI fallback for this section
  RETURN (null, level: 3)
```

### UI Degradation Rules

| Eligible Count | UI Behavior |
|---------------|-------------|
| ≥ 4 | Show 4 cards, user picks 1 |
| 3 | Show 3 cards, user picks 1 |
| 2 | Show 2 cards, user picks 1 |
| 1 | Show 1 card, auto-selected with info banner |
| 0 | Section generated by AI fallback; show AI-generated card with "✨ AI" badge |

